[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1119,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 1158,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155065,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1158,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxoinflammatory fibroblastic sarcoma is an intermediate, rarely metastasizing neoplasm showing both a predilection for acral sites and variably myxoid and cellular areas with bland spindle cells, a prominent inflammatory infiltrate, and scattered large polygonal cells with macronucleoli.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1120,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 1159,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155066,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1159,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8811/1 Myxoinflammatory fibroblastic sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1121,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1160,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155067,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1160,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B5F.2 &amp; XH2D15 Sarcoma, not elsewhere classified of other specified sites &amp; Myxoinflammatory fibroblastic sarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1122,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155068,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1161,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1123,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155069,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1124,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155070,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour presents most often in the acral sites: hands, fingers, and feet, more often on dorsal sides. Rarely it presents in the proximal parts of extremities and trunk wall {9578090; 9706971; 24121178; 25886867}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1125,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155071,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour typically forms a raised mass on hands or feet and is typically wider than deep. It can mimic an inflammatory process. Local recurrence is common, but metastases are exceedingly rare {24121178}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1126,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155072,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is rare and predominantly occurs in young to middle-aged adults with a slight female predominance. Isolated cases have been reported in children and adolescents aged 5&ndash;17&nbsp;years {9578090; 9706971; 24121178; 25886867; 23919754; 32514165}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1127,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155073,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1128,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155074,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>TGFBR3</em>::<em>OGA</em> (<em>MGEA5</em>) fusions have been detected in 32&ndash;80% of cases. Similar fusions and histological overlap between myxoinflammatory fibroblastic tumour and pleomorphic hyaline angiectatic tumour have prompted discussion about whether these tumours are related or are part of one entity {21717526; 26980036; 29979612; 26626209}. <em>BRAF</em> fusions are seen in as many as 30% of cases, and <em>VGLL3</em> amplification is common, especially in connection with a <em>BRAF</em> fusion {28692601; 31898851; 32514165; 39822017}. Rarely, other fusions have been reported: <em>SND1</em>::<em>BRAF</em>, <em>SEC23IP</em>::<em>VGLL3</em>, and <em>TEAD1</em>::<em>MRTFB</em> {35776191}. Nodular necrotizing fibroblastic tumour, which shows morphological overlap with myxoinflammatory fibroblastic sarcoma, has <em>YAP1</em>::<em>MAML2</em> fusions {35546636}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1135,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155075,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are often lobulated and can be gelatinous, fleshy, or firm. Size varies from 15&nbsp;to &gt;&nbsp;200&nbsp;mm, and the average size is 30&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1129,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155076,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour contains large polygonal cells with nuclear pleomorphism, pseudoinclusions, and large eosinophilic nucleoli, potentially mimicking Hodgkin cells. Vacuolated pseudolipoblasts and mildly atypical spindle cells are often seen. There is a prominent stromal lymphoplasmacytic and neutrophilic inflammatory component. Cellularity is moderate to high in half of the cases. Mitoses are usually rare: &lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> (equivalent to &lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mitoses/50&nbsp;HPF of 0.5&nbsp;mm diameter and 0.2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> area), and only 10% of cases have &gt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> (&gt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mitoses/50&nbsp;HPF of 0.5&nbsp;mm diameter and 0.2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> area). Stroma is mostly collagenous, usually with at least focal myxoid areas. Stromal haemosiderin deposition is common, and some cases have areas reminiscent of haemosiderotic fibrolipomatous tumour. Half of the cases are positive for CD34, while there is less common (10&ndash;15%) positivity for desmin, EMA, and keratin cocktail {24121178; 32514165; 9706971; 9578090}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1130,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155077,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Diagnosis on cytology is difficult, but the tissue fragments of myxoid and collagenous matrix containing a mix of bland spindle cells, polygonal/epithelioid cells, and occasional atypical Reed&ndash;Sternberg&ndash;like cells with macronucleoli, along with inflammatory cells and haemosiderin, can provide a provisional diagnosis {33431307}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1131,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155078,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1134,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155079,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> variably myxoid and cellular areas with bland spindle cells, a prominent inflammatory infiltrate, and scattered large polygonal cells with macronucleoli.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1132,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155080,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1133,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155081,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 44,
        "headingId": 1172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>About half of the patients experience a local recurrence, and some have multiple recurrences. Distant metastasis is very uncommon (~1%).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T15:05:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]